==Problem==

Square <imath>ABCD</imath> has side length <imath>1</imath>. Points <imath>P</imath>, <imath>Q</imath>, <imath>R</imath>, and <imath>S</imath> each lie on a side of <imath>ABCD</imath> such that <imath>APQCRS</imath> is an equilateral convex hexagon with side length <imath>s</imath>. What is <imath>s</imath>?

<imath>\textbf{(A) } \frac{\sqrt{2}}{3} \qquad \textbf{(B) } \frac{1}{2} \qquad \textbf{(C) } 2 - \sqrt{2} \qquad \textbf{(D) } 1 - \frac{\sqrt{2}}{4} \qquad \textbf{(E) } \frac{2}{3}</imath>

== Diagram ==
